From: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
Subject: i386: do not hang in PIT TSC calibration on broken speaker ports

On PC BIOS, grub_machine_init() calibrates the TSC from PIT channel 2
before printing "Welcome to GRUB!". grub_pit_wait() spins until port
0x61 bit 5 (OUT) goes high.

On some chipsets and firmwares that bit never changes: the wait is an
infinite loop. The user sees the boot.S "GRUB " banner (and maybe
diskboot's "loading") and then a blinking cursor forever. Other
machines, with a working PIT, continue normally.

Cap the wait with a TSC delta and an I/O iteration limit, then fall
through to the hardcoded rate. Do not call the ACPI PM timer from the
i386-pc kernel: that object lives in the random module, not kernel.img.

---
 grub-core/kern/i386/tsc_pit.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/grub-core/kern/i386/tsc_pit.c b/grub-core/kern/i386/tsc_pit.c
--- a/grub-core/kern/i386/tsc_pit.c
+++ b/grub-core/kern/i386/tsc_pit.c
@@ -51,8 +51,28 @@ grub_pit_wait (void)
 
   if ((grub_inb (GRUB_PIT_SPEAKER_PORT) & GRUB_PIT_SPK_TMR2_LATCH) == 0x00) {
     ret = 1;
-    /* Wait.  */
-    while ((grub_inb (GRUB_PIT_SPEAKER_PORT) & GRUB_PIT_SPK_TMR2_LATCH) == 0x00);
+    /*
+     * Wait for the 55ms countdown. Some firmwares leave bit 5 of port
+     * 0x61 stuck at 0, so this must not spin forever: that hangs BIOS
+     * boot after the "GRUB " banner and before the menu.
+     *
+     * 4e9 TSC ticks is ~400ms at 10GHz / ~2s at 2GHz, well above 55ms.
+     * The iteration cap covers a frozen TSC.
+     */
+    {
+      grub_uint64_t start_tsc = grub_get_tsc ();
+      grub_uint32_t iters = 0;
+
+      while ((grub_inb (GRUB_PIT_SPEAKER_PORT) & GRUB_PIT_SPK_TMR2_LATCH) == 0x00)
+	{
+	  if (++iters > 0x1000000UL
+	      || grub_get_tsc () - start_tsc > 4000000000ULL)
+	    {
+	      ret = 0;
+	      break;
+	    }
+	}
+    }
   }
 
   /* Disable timer2 gate and speaker.  */
